From efe1cefcc9d66e384627aa3d7c4c758c17a03ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tessera CI <ci@tessera.test>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:21:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ml): point-in-time card_chargeback_rate and the
 fraud pipeline

Every historical aggregate takes an explicit as_of and only counts what had happened by it: chargebacks filed before the cutoff over transactions before the cutoff, strict inequality, so a row never sees itself. The pipeline binds the aggregate to the scoring-timestamp cutoff, the one under which the fraud-v3 shadow feature stats reproduce exactly (non-zero share 0.1419), and strips the label before any feature function runs.

Notebook 01 computed this feature over the whole table and reported 0.906 AUC; point-in-time it is 0.778, the champion. TESS-2310.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
