Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:21:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(ml): implement the four model-validation gates with
 a negative leakage fixture

Gate 1 recomputes every feature with future disputes hidden and with each row own dispute hidden, and fails if any value moves. Gate 2 floors PR-AUC on a temporal split at the review budget, by month, next to the champion. Gate 3 uses mass-point-aware PSI so a 97%-zero feature cannot hide a quadrupled non-zero share in a single quantile bin. Gate 4 writes per-slice metrics with FPR and flag-rate ratios and marks four-fifths breaches for review.

Each module takes exactly the flags in model-validation.yml. The notebook-01 definition of card_chargeback_rate is kept in ml/validation/tests/leaky_fixtures.py on purpose; test_leakage.py proves Gate 1 fails on it and test_performance.py shows it clears any floor, which is why Gate 1 runs first. TESS-2310.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
